{"id": "EUVD-2026-103837", "enisaUuid": "5a6a338b-1650-35d1-8d59-0edd157a5296", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ntty: port: fix tty_port_tty_vhangup() race\n\nDrivers rely on tty_port_tty_vhangup() to synchronously hang up their\nports before tearing down resources as part of deregistration (e.g. on\nphysical disconnect).\n\nIf tty_port_tty_vhangup() races with another hangup it may however\nreturn before the port has been shut down. This is in turn can lead to\nuse-after-free and NULL-pointer dereferences in racing ioctls (including\na synchronous hangup) and in processing of racing asynchronous hangups\n(carrier loss).\n\nAdd the missing serialisation to tty_port_tty_vhangup() and\ntty_port_hangup() so that the former does not return until the port has\nbeen shut down also when there is a racing hangup.\n\nNote that serial core does not use tty_port_hangup(), but it already\nholds the port mutex when clearing port->tty and shutting down the port\nin uart_hangup().", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:47:36", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:56:27", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ce220b4cdf62f73db0c1940f968eb33b9899fdd0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6d1a984afc3ca477dab3e51ec806671d443ad524", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6b7be3b9b857947e9c1338d4919d4ebd3b75e907", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/017b18addbe8dcace1a569a00d40ed1ba1e03f4c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b48820de8c1a596c5b99775524dfce73c6576c5d"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98752", "GHSA-2697-8gj7-2gh6"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0ee19de5-a6c3-36b5-b330-a3518f53baa7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "3d4c4258-652d-3c7d-a918-17595e386ee3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4260dc792fabfd20c8644fa9414b2ae48372365f"}, {"id": "6024b80e-505e-3d88-b33b-1554acb769fa", "produ